Hi Both, me too!

Some reproducible code (from an older SO post <http://stackoverflow.com/questions/26613181/r-shiny-app-using-ggvis-gives-error-during-upload>, slightly edited with fixes):

## ui.R
library(ggvis)

shinyUI(bootstrapPage(
  ggvisOutput("ggvis"),
  uiOutput("ggvis_ui")
))

## server.R
library(ggvis)

shinyServer(function(input, output, session) {
  input_width <- reactive(input$width)

  mtcars %>%
    ggvis(~mpg) %>%
    layer_histograms(width = input_width) %>%
    bind_shiny("ggvis", "ggvis_ui")
})

## When located in folder with ui.R and server.R file:
library("shiny")
library("shinyapps")
runApp()  # works fine locally
deployApp()  # error message

With deployApp(), I see the same error message as in the subject line of the previous posts. It is the next console message after ## End Log ##, (i.e. after installing packages and copying files). This happens both with the above reproducible example and my own Shiny App code.

Andrew

